WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.920
Five junctions, eight
streets, and one postman.

2
00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:06.110
Each street has its length marked.

3
00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:11.720
Four, six, seven, three,
eight, five, four, ten.

4
00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:13.970
Added up, that's forty-seven.

5
00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:18.550
He must walk every street at least
once and return to the sorting office.

6
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.820
He sets off, and soon
he's stuck: to finish,

7
00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:23.660
he must repeat a street.

8
00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.110
So what's the shortest possible route?

9
00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:27.410
Is it forty-seven?

10
00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.470
Twice that?

11
00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:29.960
And how would you know?

12
00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:33.170
In this mission, you'll treat
the village as a weighted graph,

13
00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:35.130
and find its total weight.

14
00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:38.290
You'll learn why vertices
of odd degree cause trouble,

15
00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:41.100
and find the shortest
path between two vertices,

16
00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:43.560
even when it isn't the direct edge.

17
00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:46.920
Your mission: find the
shortest route for the postman.
